A||||2||GodSend||A few bugs to work out with my 87 GT||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||09-01-2000||11:18 AM||||  Ive only had my baby for about 3 weeks, and love it to death, There are however a few things I wanted to inquire about.<P>a]  My drivers side door seems to open and close fine.  It hits the lock striker perfect (does not scrape).  When you look at all the gaps between the door and the body panels they line up perfect.<P>  To spite this whenever I hit anything above a tiny bump the drivers door jumps up and down a little (I always drive with my arm on the rest, so I notice it).  When I try to move the door when its closed it seems firm as can be, Any ideas?<P>b]  Both my driver and passanger windows seem to let some air when totally rolled up at about shoulder height.  Ive checked the rubber around the window and it seems in place and fine. Any ideas?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (see a trend)<P>c]  My fuel pump seems to stay on for maybe 1 or 2 seconds after shutting the car down, its this normal?<P>d]  My passanger tailpipe hangs down a little lower then my drivers side.  I have not had an opportunity to jack er up yet to look under.  I did however grab the pipe and its solid as can be, wont move, and is not bent.  I have never inspected the exhaust system so I have no idea how to go about adjusting.<P>  Thanks for your help, pics coming real soon.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-01-2000||11:03 PM||||Hmmm. The only one I can really help you with right now is the fuel pump staying on after the car is shut off. It just happened to my Formula. Its your oil sending unit. Change it! or itll get to the point to where the pump keeps running until the battery dies. <BR>Its an EXTREMELY simple fix, and they usually run from 20-30 dollars at autozone.<BR>I have to give credit to the forum dudes for that one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||09-02-2000||05:45 AM||||For the door I'd check the hinge pins to make sure there in all the way. If they are then I'd make sure the bolts that hold the hinges themselves to the chassis are not loose. I bet this may be the reason some air gets in when the windows are rolled up all the way as well.<BR> The exhaust tips are clamped on to the exhaust system about a foot down from the tip. I'd either make sure your not missing any springs holding the exhaust up, if not loosen the clamp holding the tip, adjust it to right height, re-tighten.<BR> I can hear my fuel pump turn on for a few seconds BEFORE I start the car. I've never heard it after I shut her down so I'd take My7Fiero's advice on that one.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||3
